@* The renderer.
The renderer is the only part of the program that speaks Direct3D~11 at length. Its job
is modest: create the device and the window's swap chain, compile the shaders, keep one
GPU mesh per shape, and draw the scene into an off-screen image that the user interface
then displays inside a panel. It knows nothing about the user interface, and the user
interface knows nothing about Direct3D except the image it receives.

