@ This structure is the C++ image of the constant buffer of \S\ref{cbuffer}. Each line
of four values is one 16-byte row of the buffer; the |static_assert| catches the most
common mistake, a structure whose size is not a multiple of a row.

<<Constants of a frame, as seen from C++>>=
// Mirrors cbuffer Frame in shaders/pbr.hlsl (16-byte aligned rows).
struct FrameConstants {
    DirectX::XMFLOAT4X4 world;
    DirectX::XMFLOAT4X4 viewProj;
    DirectX::XMFLOAT3 cameraPos;  float bumpStrength;
    DirectX::XMFLOAT3 lightPos;   float lightIntensity;
    DirectX::XMFLOAT3 lightColor; float dispScale;
    float dispMid, dispLod, metallic, ambient;
    int viewMode, useColor, useBump, useDisp;
    int useRough; float constRoughness; DirectX::XMFLOAT2 hoverUV;
    float hoverOn; DirectX::XMFLOAT3 pad;
};
static_assert(sizeof(FrameConstants) % 16 == 0);

@ Lines are given as pairs of vertices with a colour each.

<<Vertices of lines>>=
struct LineVertex {
    DirectX::XMFLOAT3 pos;
    DirectX::XMFLOAT4 color;
};

@ The public interface follows the life of a frame: |BeginFrame| prepares the window for
the user interface, |RenderScene| draws the 3D view off-screen, |Present| shows the
result. The number of segments per patch is public because the user interface needs it
to choose the mipmap level for displacement.

<<Public interface of the renderer>>=
